Spec: n/a (chore — spawned follow-up from the npm test single-file-selection fix)
Task: Delete test:quick per Peter's decision
Agent: Claude (main session)
Unit: this chore (single commit)

## What

- Removes the root `test:quick` script from package.json.
- Adds dated removal notes to the two historical docs that documented it
  (`.kiro/specs/release-analysis-system/test-command-implementation.md`,
  `performance-test-analysis.md`) — records preserved, not rewritten.

## Why deletion (Peter's call, offered delete vs. lane-config fix)

- Same footgun as the `npm test` one fixed in #97: trailing array-typed
  `--testPathIgnorePatterns` means `npm run test:quick -- <file>` ADDS the file
  as an ignore pattern instead of selecting it.
- Unused: no CI workflow, hook, or steering doc references it — only two
  historical spec docs.
- Rationale void: since the 2026-07-03 lane rework (`29bba7de`), `test:quick`
  was just `npm test` minus the integration suites on a ~1-minute lane;
  skipping integration coverage invites false-green validation.

## Validation

- `npm test`: 367/367 suites, 8891 tests passed.
- The `test` script string is byte-unchanged, so lane selection cannot shift.
- package.json parses; no remaining operational `test:quick` references
  (remaining hits are historical records, now annotated).

## Flagged, NOT fixed here (out of scope)

The revert `f4e40cef` mis-resolved and left DUPLICATE `test:performance` and
`test:performance:isolated` keys in package.json (visible in this diff's
context lines). Values are identical so behavior is unaffected (last-wins),
but the duplication is unintended. Left untouched to keep this chore's diff
faithful to the original; needs a separate call.

